<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- BIO-INT-004 owns api/features/bio-int-004/** only. No ProjectReference to
         Biolog.Api.csproj (one-way dependency, scripts/check-module-project-references.sh)
         and none to any sibling feature project either - not bio-rpt-001 (IDomainEventBus/
         DomainEventEnvelope), not bio-idn-006 (permission grants), not bio-int-003 (actor-
         provenance precedent this story's own Api/ActorProvenanceGate.cs duplicates by value).
         api/Biolog.Api/Modules/BioInt004Module.cs is the one place that can see more than one
         of these projects at once, and is where the real IDomainEventBus subscription and the
         DomainEventEnvelope -> WebhookEventEnvelope translation both live (the same
         host-module translation-boundary shape BioDev003Module's CertificationGateAdapter
         already established for an analogous cross-feature-type boundary).

         Domain/WebhookEventEnvelope.cs is this project's own documented copy of BIO-ARC-003's
         event-envelope shape (contracts/schemas/event-envelope.schema.json) - a THIRD
         independent duplicate after BIO-RPT-001's own DomainEventEnvelope.cs and BIO-DEV-003's
         DeviceDescriptor, the same "duplicate the minimal shape" boundary pattern this
         codebase already established, not an accidental drift risk.

         No JWT/session ADR exists anywhere in this codebase (confirmed by search before
         designing, same as every sibling story's own csproj comment). Webhook delivery
         signatures here are a hand-rolled HMAC-SHA256 over the raw request body plus a
         timestamp (Domain/WebhookSigner.cs), the same shape BIO-INT-001's
         HmacSessionTokenCodec/BIO-IDN-006's ActorProvenanceGate/BIO-INT-003's
         HmacApiAccessTokenCodec already established - not a JWT library dependency. -->
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Biolog.Api" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Biolog.Features.Webhooks.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
